        "title": "Amphibia - The Water-to-Land Transition",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "420 Ma   Lobe-finned fish (Eusthenopteron) — fins with bone\n          Shallow water, swampy habitats\n375 Ma   TIKTAALIK ROSEAE\n          Fins with humerus, radius/ulna, proto-wrist\n          Could raise head (neck present)\n          Could prop body off substrate\n365 Ma   ACANTHOSTEGA (Greenland)\n          8-fingered limbs (more than tetrapod standard!)\n          Still largely aquatic\n          Limbs used for locomotion IN WATER first\n          Gills still present\n365 Ma   ICHTHYOSTEGA (Greenland)\n          7-fingered limbs\n          Could make short terrestrial excursions\n          Heavy ribs → some weight support on land\n360 Ma   Terrestrial tetrapods establishing\n          5-digit limbs now standard\n340 Ma   First amniotes (Carboniferous)"
    }
